            0.149
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) Discuss with your family members to decide how you will collect and organise the data."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.244,
            0.149,
            0.745,
            0.167
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(c) Collect expense data for at least 3 months."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.242,
            0.168,
            0.881,
            0.225
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(d) Represent the data in a 100% stacked bar chart, with each bar showing how the total monthly expenditure is divided across the different categories."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.244,
            0.225,
            0.881,
            0.264
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(e) Finally, write your observations and inferences based on the chart."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.275,
            0.883,
            0.372
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Small-group project:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Make a group of 3–4 students. Choose one scenario to design a custom rating scheme by assigning appropriate weights: (a) shopping experience at a cloth store, (b) travel experience in a bus, (c) tourism experience of a nearby tourist spot, (d) clinic/hospital experience"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.195,
            0.375,
            0.881,
            0.413
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Discuss and arrive at 4–6 aspects to rate. For each aspect chosen, justify why it matters for an overall experience."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.413,
            0.787,
            0.433
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Discuss and decide the relative weights and justify."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.432,
            0.881,
            0.471
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Collect or imagine ratings from at least 10 people on a scale of 1–5 (5 being very good)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.184,
            0.471,
            0.881,
            0.509
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) Compute each individual rating. Compute the overall average across individuals."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.509,
            0.755,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(v) Make a 100% stacked bar chart using your data."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.184,
            0.528,
            0.882,
            0.569
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(vi) Write a short note on the observations and inferences, what your rating system captures well and what it misses."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.577,
            0.884,
            0.655
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "14. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Whole class project:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Each student shares the average age of their family and the number of family members. Discuss among the class and come up with a way to find out the average age of all the families of the class."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.659,
            0.883,
            0.758
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*15. Given some data with corresponding weights, what would happen to the weighted average if all the weights are increased by a constant value, say 1? If required, experiment with some data. What do you observe? Justify your answer using algebra."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
