          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.761,
            0.883,
            0.86
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*16. A farm has some cows, sheep, and chickens. Last year the cows made up 60%, the sheep 25%, and the chickens 15%. There was a decrease in the number of all three animals’ population over the year. Choose the possibilities for the change in their respective shares of the population —"
            }
          ]
        }
